BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture360-asef-arts-in-the-wake-of-ai-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260917T095954Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: culture360 / ASEF: Call for Content\, Arts in the Wake of
  AI (SGD 250 per commission)
DESCRIPTION:culture360.ASEF.org\, the arts platform of the Asia-Europe Foun
 dation\, invites proposals from writers and content producers for its open
  call 'Arts in the Wake of AI': articles\, podcasts and video interviews t
 hat foreground how cultural professionals and organisations across Asia an
 d Europe are adapting to AI technologies\, from generative tools and machi
 ne learning to recommender systems and algorithms. WHAT THEY WANT: case-st
 udy-based contributions grounded in real-world evidence\, experiences or p
 ractices\, on topics including the impact of AI on cultural diversity\, fa
 irness and inclusivity\; the environmental costs of AI in the cultural sec
 tor\; and AI governance in the cultural sector (policy\, copyright\, intel
 lectual property and the ethical use of AI-generated cultural content). Ac
 ademic research papers and non-arts subjects are not considered. FEE: SGD 
 250 per commissioned article\, podcast or video interview. FORMATS: journa
 listic articles of 800 to 1\,000 words with at least four credited images\
 ; podcasts and video interviews of 15 to 20 minutes. ELIGIBILITY: national
 s of ASEM partner countries with previous experience in writing\, podcasti
 ng or video production\, proficiency in English\, and knowledge of or invo
 lvement in the Asian and European arts and culture scene\; an existing cha
 nnel for further dissemination is an advantage\; the work is fully virtual
 . Up to two proposals per application. Only selected writers are notified.
  Queries to culture[at]asef.org. Deadline 29 September 2026 at 6 PM Singap
 ore time\, via the online application form.\n\nOrganisation: Asia-Europe F
 oundation (ASEF)\, culture360.ASEF.org\nLocation: Fully remote\; contribut
 ors do not need to be based in Singapore. Open to nationals of ASEM partne
 r countries across Asia and Europe.\nAward: SGD 250 fee per commissioned a
 rticle\, podcast or video interview. Up to two proposals per application\,
  of which at most one is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off 
 editorial commissions: articles of 800 to 1\,000 words with at least four 
 credited pictures\, podcasts and video interviews of 15 to 20 minutes\n\nM
 ore: https://culture360.asef.org/opportunities/call-for-content-arts-ai/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture360.asef.org/opportunities/call-for-content-arts-ai/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fully remote\; contributors do not need to be based in Singapore. 
 Open to nationals of ASEM partner countries across Asia and Europe.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260917T095954Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sloan-foundation-book-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260917T095954Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alfred P. Sloan Foundation: Book Grants (Public Understan
 ding of Science and Technology)
DESCRIPTION:The one Sloan program that funds individuals directly: grants f
 or authors researching and writing nonfiction books that bring science and
  technology to a general audience. Over 200 authors supported since 1996. 
 Favoured topics include elucidating confusing or controversial scientific 
 subjects\, profiles of figures in science and technology\, science-technol
 ogy-art connections\, women and science\, and the culture and philosophy o
 f science. Start with a letter of inquiry to program director Doron Weber\
 ; full proposals are by invitation only. Reviewed three times a year: LOIs
  by 1 September (decision by 15 February)\, 1 January (by 31 May) and 1 Ma
 y (by 31 October). No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Alfred P. Sloan Fo
 undation\nLocation: Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directl
 y to authors or via a nonprofit host)\nAward: Typically up to $60\,000 per
  book grant\nDuration: Project-based (book research and writing)\n\nMore: 
 https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directly to authors
  or via a nonprofit host)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stigler-center-journalists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260917T095954Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stigler Center: Journalists in Residence Program Spring 2
 027 (Chicago Booth\; USD 14\,000 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:The Stigler Center at the University of Chicago Booth School of
  Business invites journalists from around the world to its Journalists in 
 Residence Program\, a roughly 12-week residency on the Hyde Park campus in
  spring 2027 focused on the interactions between politics\, business\, mar
 kets and the economy. Running since 2017\, the program has hosted journali
 sts from outlets including the BBC\, The New York Times and ABC News. WHAT
  YOU DO: audit three Chicago Booth classes\, participate actively in class
  discussions and complete required readings and assignments\, attend Stigl
 er Center seminars\, lectures\, conferences and other activities\, collabo
 rate with peers\, network with faculty and researchers\, and explore oppor
 tunities to write for the Center's ProMarket publication. WHAT YOU GET: US
 D 14\,000 stipend for living expenses\, economy-class airfare reimbursemen
 t\, SEVIS and visa application fee coverage\, health insurance through UCh
 icago\, housing guidance\, academic opportunities and a certificate upon c
 ompletion. Note that the stipend is subject to up to 14 percent tax withho
 lding for international participants and arrives after roughly the first m
 onth\, so you need funds to bridge that period. ELIGIBILITY: open to journ
 alists from all countries and media backgrounds\, including freelancers an
 d editors\, with some years of professional experience\, proficiency in En
 glish and a genuine interest in political economy and business reporting. 
 Successful applicants are notified by the end of December 2026. DEADLINE: 
 20 September 2026\, 11:59 pm Chicago time (CT).\n\nOrganisation: Stigler C
 enter\, University of Chicago Booth School of Business\nLocation: Universi
 ty of Chicago Booth School of Business\, Hyde Park campus\, Chicago\, USA.
  Open to journalists from all countries and media backgrounds.\nAward: USD
  14\,000 stipend to cover living expenses over the 12-week program\, plus 
 reimbursement of economy-class airfare to and from Chicago\, SEVIS and vis
 a application fees\, health insurance through UChicago\, and housing guida
 nce. The stipend is subject to up to 14 percent tax withholding for intern
 ational participants\, and you need sufficient funds for roughly the first
  month before the stipend arrives. No application fee.\nDuration: Approxim
 ately 12 weeks\, tentatively 15 March to 31 May 2027\n\nMore: https://www.
 chicagobooth.edu/research/stigler/education/journalists-in-residence-progr
 am?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.chicagobooth.edu/research/stigler/education/journalists-in-
 residence-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:University of Chicago Booth School of Business\, Hyde Park campus\
 , Chicago\, USA. Open to journalists from all countries and media backgrou
 nds.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
